            {
                "entry_id": "4e374320-c0a2-39cf-ab9c-2ceb3f92aef6",
                "word": "marouette",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8f52115f-00ba-4982-bc32-599d80de06f5",
                        "entry_id": "4e374320-c0a2-39cf-ab9c-2ceb3f92aef6",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "marouettes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c71f5500-9a36-3484-9962-9df14fc3b7f9",
                        "entry_id": "4e374320-c0a2-39cf-ab9c-2ceb3f92aef6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petit échassier migrateur, voisin des râles, de la famille des rallidés."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3ed86aa-1ce2-4c9a-bfbf-adecad70c24a",
                                "sense_id": "c71f5500-9a36-3484-9962-9df14fc3b7f9",
                                "text": "La marouette, qu'il est impossible de confondre avec aucun des genres voisins, est un oiseau de passage dont l’émigration périodique et régulière commence et finit chaque année avec celle des cailles, et dure deux mois environ, de la mi-août à la mi-octobre. Elle abonde alors suivant les années dans les pays d'étang, dans les prairies marécageuses et dans les mares des plaines."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49f9b0cc-eb40-4943-a733-f88c7e636a93",
                                "sense_id": "c71f5500-9a36-3484-9962-9df14fc3b7f9",
                                "text": "Le pré dégageait une odeur de terreau humide, une marouette sifflait dans les roseaux au sud. Son chant sonnait comme des gouttes d'eau qui tombaient."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "539624ed-8684-3728-a1de-9c46e74a6fae",
                        "entry_id": "4e374320-c0a2-39cf-ab9c-2ceb3f92aef6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Un des noms vernaculaires de l’anthémis fétide, dite aussi marute."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d280d5eb-416f-4d7c-abc2-4b07c1a408a2",
                                "sense_id": "539624ed-8684-3728-a1de-9c46e74a6fae",
                                "text": "Maroute (ou marouette): nom vulgaire de la camomille puante, utilisée pendant la guerre pour la fabrication des produits pharmaceutiques. (Plante qui abondait dans les cours de ferme, et que pour se faire quelques sous, les gamins allaient vendre aux pharmacien du coin.)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e6533267-e218-4884-a45a-9a0eeaf9a5cd",
                        "source_entry_id": "4e374320-c0a2-39cf-ab9c-2ceb3f92aef6",
                        "target_lang_word": "Sumpfhuhn",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e149a100-9e7d-484d-a72f-1c246fe45d2d",
                        "source_entry_id": "4e374320-c0a2-39cf-ab9c-2ceb3f92aef6",
                        "target_lang_word": "crake",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "crake",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b514180d-dadd-3f99-b9b2-48e094339f1a",
                                        "entry_id": "1655d41d-ac0a-35a8-b7cc-d23172f88acc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several birds of the family Rallidae that have short bills."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "crake",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b28a6169-8446-39e2-a794-3565d343474a",
                                        "entry_id": "c235f068-82fd-36a7-9b99-c7209687258a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cry out harshly and loudly, like a crake."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f62c0082-9d5d-43ae-a4b3-cf761f5b8389",
                                                "sense_id": "b28a6169-8446-39e2-a794-3565d343474a",
                                                "text": "How still ! how very still it is, So silent it appears, E'en from its intensity, To tingle in mine ears. I hear the sheep-bell far away In the calm breathless night; The corncrake begins to crake . Crake, crake, with all its might."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a70ba5a-1984-429f-9514-830e77203eda",
                                                "sense_id": "b28a6169-8446-39e2-a794-3565d343474a",
                                                "text": "'How very disagreeable!' said Annie; 'perhaps the birds took it in turn to crake.'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a892509c-3e89-4494-9f07-5cd4ecead632",
                                                "sense_id": "b28a6169-8446-39e2-a794-3565d343474a",
                                                "text": "Of course, a corncrake, as its name suggests, likes to crake among the corn and hayfields, so that in fact you are unlikely ever to confuse it with the spotted crake, a bird to which dry land is almost anathema."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "crake",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d503c67f-d877-3165-b716-6c2445d24cde",
                                        "entry_id": "671abf37-1cde-3426-ae88-87cec0dea8bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To boast; to speak loudly and boastfully."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fab99d1a-d454-4b15-80e1-3e3cf7aa9f84",
                                                "sense_id": "d503c67f-d877-3165-b716-6c2445d24cde",
                                                "text": "I hyred the to fyght agaynste Alexander, and not to crake and prate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b01bd040-4a84-4736-8c08-005966f2a924",
                                                "sense_id": "d503c67f-d877-3165-b716-6c2445d24cde",
                                                "text": "Each man may crake of that which was his own."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d026612-bd12-48aa-877c-82e52eb74c15",
                                                "sense_id": "d503c67f-d877-3165-b716-6c2445d24cde",
                                                "text": "With him I threatned to be quite, and great things did I crake."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55a6d847-4839-42b6-b9b5-644e53ecfe74",
                                                "sense_id": "d503c67f-d877-3165-b716-6c2445d24cde",
                                                "text": "And he that thus doth shal have smal pleasure in his awn rightwysnes, nor no gret lust to crake of his awn deserts or meryts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "crake",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf0d6576-5f5b-3b69-af26-941648e5a449",
                                        "entry_id": "5e373432-b813-383a-a5cc-02220783ef25",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crack; a boast."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
